.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Local agent and editor config: the dev-server entry that serves this folder
# on a port, and whatever else lands beside it. Machine-specific, and nothing
# here is needed to build, serve, or read the app.
.claude/

# Generated by scripts/pilot.mjs during review, not worth committing.
art/pilot/*/crops/
art/pilot/*/sheet.html
art/pilot/masters.html

# The working rounds: every generation, kept or rejected, as it arrived.
# Rounds 1-19 (264 MB, all superseded) were deleted on 2026-08-12 — what they
# taught is written down in §7 of docs/illustration-audit.md and in the batch
# post-mortems in docs/pilot-prompts.md, which is the part worth keeping.
# Numbering was not reset, because those post-mortems cite rounds by number.
#
# art/pilot/approved/ IS committed: those are the masters every shipped image
# is generated against, and until they were committed they existed on one
# laptop. Never add them to this list.
art/pilot/round-*/

# The restyle rounds, same reasoning, own counter. Kept apart from round-*/
# because rounds 1-19 are the tan-era set and are cited by number in the
# post-mortems; continuing that numbering would make every citation ambiguous.
# The generated review artefacts sit one level deeper here than they did, so
# the two rules above do not reach them.
art/pilot/restyle/

# Secrets. The image pipeline reads OPENAI_API_KEY from the environment, and
# the local command supplies it with `node --env-file=.env.local`. That file is
# real credentials and must never be committed; the example carries key names
# only and is safe to track.
.env*
!.env.example
